From 3b992220fa565edde240011e15cfe9210fff1e54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:37:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban): move switcher counts per changed task on the P2
 cursor [daveey]

Card E stage8 (t_78d2b488ee11aa70). The stage7 scale matrix failed one gate:
a changed board's GET /boards on a 440 MB WAL grew 5.347 -> 8.057 ms from 1k to
20k tasks (1.507x > 1.5x), because every changed board was re-counted with a
whole-table GROUP BY status on a fresh connection.

board_counts now keeps each board's task statuses and the P2 cursor they were
read at. A changed board reads changed_since and the status of only those tasks
in one snapshot and moves each between buckets (insert, status move, delete).
FULL (first read, new file/WAL generation, schema, older-writer trigger), more
than DELTA_MAX changes, or a failed read take the whole-board read; a legacy
board without a cursor keeps the exact GROUP BY. The entry is unpublished while
it is updated under a per-board lock, so a failure leaves nothing stale.

Tests: test_kanban_board_counts_delta.py (3 RED on base, 6 GREEN); 16 dashboard
suites, 181 tests GREEN. Scale matrix (real ASGI, 1k/5.8k/20k, checkpointed and
440 MB WAL): changed-list 6.1/6.3/5.9 ms on WAL (0.97x), 5.4/5.9/5.9 ms
checkpointed (1.10x); all ten gated scenarios pass, and the runner now exits
nonzero on any failed gate (control: stage7 results -> exit 1).
